.TH JOSHCONFIG 1 "June 2026" "joshconfig 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
joshconfig \- manage PATH and MANPATH environment variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B joshconfig
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B joshconfig
.BR \-\-version
.RB | \-V
.PP
.B joshconfig
.BR \-\-help
.RB | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B joshconfig
extracts PATH and MANPATH modifications from shell configuration files and
creates individual entry files in ~/.paths.d/ and ~/.manpaths.d/. A lightweight
Rust binary (joshconfig-env) reads these entries at shell startup via a sourced
shim script, providing deduplication and consistent path management.
.PP
The tool uses two methods to extract PATH modifications:
.IP \(bu 2
Static parsing: Regex-based extraction of PATH= and MANPATH= assignments
.IP \(bu 2
Dynamic instrumentation: Spawns shell processes with tracing to capture
actual runtime values
.SH COMMANDS
.SS analyze
Analyze shell configuration files and generate .paths.d/.manpaths.d entries.
.PP
.B joshconfig analyze
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-shell
.IR shell ]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be generated without writing files
.TP
.BR \-\-shell =\fIshell\fR
Specify which shell to analyze (bash, zsh, or both). Default: both
.PP
This command:
.IP \(bu 2
Scans shell config files (~/.bash_profile, ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Extracts PATH and MANPATH assignments
.IP \(bu 2
Creates numbered entry files in ~/.paths.d/ and ~/.manpaths.d/
.IP \(bu 2
Skips entries from /etc/paths.d/ and /etc/manpaths.d/ (handled by path_helper)
.SS shellenv
Emit shell commands to set PATH and MANPATH from .paths.d/.manpaths.d.
.PP
.B joshconfig shellenv
.PP
Outputs VARIABLE=value and export VARIABLE lines for PATH and MANPATH
based on the contents of ~/.paths.d/ and ~/.manpaths.d/. Used internally
by the joshconfig-load-paths.sh shim but can also be called directly.
.SS doctor
Check and fix loader line position in shell config files.
.PP
.B joshconfig doctor
.RB [ \-\-fix ]
.RB [ \-\-shell
.IR shell ]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BR \-\-fix
Move the loader line to the end of the file if it is positioned incorrectly.
.TP
.BR \-\-shell =\fIshell\fR
Target a specific shell config file (bash or zsh). Default: both
.PP
Without --fix, only reports problems (dry-run).
.SS list
List current entries in .paths.d and .manpaths.d directories.
.PP
.B joshconfig list
.PP
Displays all managed path entries with their source files and line numbers.
.SS help
Show help information.
.PP
.B joshconfig help
.RI [ command ]
.SS GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are available for all commands:
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print version information and exit
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print help information and exit
.SS INSTALL SCRIPT
The installation script (scripts/install.sh) supports the following options:
.PP
.B scripts/install.sh
.RB [ \-\-version | \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-help | \-h ]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print the installation script version and exit
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print help information and exit
.PP
The install script is compatible with GNU bash version 3.2.57 and later.
.SH ENTRY FILE FORMAT
Each file in ~/.paths.d/ or ~/.manpaths.d/ contains one path entry:
.PP
.nf
/path/to/directory # Optional comment
.fi
.PP
Filename format: \fINN-description\fR where \fINN\fR is a numeric prefix for
ordering (e.g., 10-homebrew-bin, 20-go-bin).
.PP
The loader reads files in alphabetical order, so numeric prefixes
control the order of path entries.
.SH LOADER SCRIPT
joshconfig installs a single loader shim (joshconfig-load-paths.sh) that works in both
zsh and bash. Source it at the end of your shell configuration:
.PP
.nf
# ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc
. "$HOME/.local/bin/joshconfig-load-paths.sh"
.fi
.PP
The shim:
.IP 1. 4
Locates the joshconfig-env binary (or falls back to joshconfig shellenv)
.IP 2. 4
Calls it and evals the emitted VARIABLE=value / export VARIABLE commands
.IP 3. 4
Warns if the loader line is not at the end of the sourcing file
.PP
The joshconfig-env binary:
.IP 1. 4
Reads all files in ~/.paths.d/ (sorted alphabetically)
.IP 2. 4
Strips comments and expands ~ and $HOME
.IP 3. 4
Prepends entries to existing PATH
.IP 4. 4
Removes duplicates while preserving order
.PP
The shim is compatible with GNU bash version 3.2.57 and later, as well as zsh.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Analyze all shell configurations
.PP
.nf
$ joshconfig analyze
Analyzing ~/.bash_profile...
Analyzing ~/.bashrc...
Analyzing ~/.zshrc...
Generated 12 entries in ~/.paths.d/
Generated 3 entries in ~/.manpaths.d/
.fi
.SS Dry run to preview changes
.PP
.nf
$ joshconfig analyze --dry-run
Would create:
  10-homebrew-bin: /opt/homebrew/bin
  20-go-bin: /usr/local/go/bin
  30-rust-bin: ~/.cargo/bin
.fi
.SS List current entries
.PP
.nf
$ joshconfig list
PATH entries:
  10-homebrew-bin: /opt/homebrew/bin
  20-go-bin: /usr/local/go/bin
  30-rust-bin: ~/.cargo/bin

MANPATH entries:
  10-homebrew-man: /opt/homebrew/share/man
.fi
.SS Check loader position (doctor)
.PP
.nf
$ joshconfig doctor
/home/user/.zshrc: loader line is correctly at the end  ✓
/home/user/.bashrc: loader line is not at the end of the file
  Line 42 (0-indexed) contains the loader, but content follows.
  Run with --fix to move it to the end.
.fi
.SS Manual entry management
.PP
.nf
# Create a new entry
$ echo "/usr/local/go/bin # Go installation" > ~/.paths.d/50-go-bin

# Edit an entry
$ vim ~/.paths.d/10-homebrew-bin

# Remove an entry
$ rm ~/.paths.d/20-old-path
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/joshconfig
Main binary
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/joshconfig-env
Standalone PATH/MANPATH emitter binary (called by loader shim)
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/joshconfig-load-paths.sh
Unified loader shim for zsh and bash
.TP
.I ~/.paths.d/
Directory containing PATH entries
.TP
.I ~/.manpaths.d/
Directory containing MANPATH entries
.TP
.I ~/.bash_profile, ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc
Shell configuration files (read-only)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate ~/.paths.d and ~/.manpaths.d
.TP
.B PATH
Modified by the loader shim
.TP
.B MANPATH
Modified by the loader shim (if ~/.manpaths.d exists)
.TP
.B JOSHCONFIG_ENV_BIN
Override path to the joshconfig-env binary (for testing or custom installs)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B joshconfig
exits with the following status codes:
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (file not found, parse error, etc.)
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments
.SH LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
No shell interpolation: Entries cannot contain complex shell expressions
.IP \(bu 2
Order dependency: Paths are prepended, so they override existing entries
.IP \(bu 2
macOS specific: Skips /etc/paths.d/ and /etc/manpaths.d/ entries
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B Error: Shell not found
The specified shell binary is not installed or not in PATH.
.TP
.B Error: Cannot read file
A shell configuration file cannot be read (permission denied or missing).
.TP
.B Warning: No PATH modifications found
The analyzed shell configuration files do not modify PATH or MANPATH.
